---

Plasma settings can be managed via GUI (systemsettings), CLI (kwriteconfig), or D-Bus (qdbus/dbus-send).

@text
kwriteconfig5 / kwriteconfig6

Read and write KDE configuration files (INI-style rc files in ~/.config/).

@code bash
# Write a config value
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key ColorScheme "BreezeDark"

# Read a config value
kreadconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key ColorScheme

# Delete a config key
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key SomeKey --delete

# Write to a specific absolute path
kwriteconfig5 --file /home/user/.config/kwinrc --group Compositing --key Backend OpenGL

# Plasma 6 equivalents
kwriteconfig6 --file kdeglobals --group General --key ColorScheme "BreezeDark"
kreadconfig6 --file kdeglobals --group General --key ColorScheme

# Common config files:
# kdeglobals        Global KDE settings (fonts, colors, toolbar style)
# kwinrc            KWin window manager settings
# plasmarc          Plasma shell settings
# kglobalshortcutsrc  Global keyboard shortcuts
# plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc  Desktop/panel widget layout
# kcminputrc        Mouse/touchpad settings
# ksmserverrc       Session management settings

@text
System Settings GUI

@code bash
# Open the full system settings application
systemsettings5
# Plasma 6
systemsettings

# Open a specific settings module directly
kcmshell5 kcm_colors          # Colors
kcmshell5 kcm_fonts           # Fonts
kcmshell5 kcm_kwinrules       # Window rules
kcmshell5 kcm_keys            # Keyboard shortcuts
kcmshell5 kcm_lookandfeel     # Global theme
kcmshell5 kcm_desktoptheme    # Plasma style
kcmshell5 kcm_icons           # Icon theme
kcmshell5 kcm_cursortheme     # Cursor theme
kcmshell5 kcm_autostart       # Autostart

# List all available KCM modules
kcmshell5 --list
# Plasma 6
kcmshell6 --list

@text
qdbus — Qt D-Bus Tool

qdbus is the Qt-native D-Bus query tool, simpler than dbus-send for KDE services.

@code bash
# List all available D-Bus services
qdbus

# List objects on a service
qdbus org.kde.KWin

# List methods on an object
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin

# Call a method
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

# Call a method with arguments
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin setCurrentDesktop 2

# Read a D-Bus property
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.currentDesktop

# Common Plasma D-Bus services:
# org.kde.KWin              Window manager
# org.kde.plasmashell        Plasma shell
# org.kde.kglobalaccel       Global shortcuts
# org.kde.ActivityManager    Activities
# org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher  System tray
# org.kde.kded5              KDE daemon
# org.freedesktop.PowerManagement  Power management

@text
dbus-send — Generic D-Bus Tool

Lower-level than qdbus, works without Qt. Use for scripts that shouldn't depend on Qt.

@code bash
# Send a D-Bus message (method call)
dbus-send --session --print-reply \
  --dest=org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.reconfigure

# Call with arguments (note type prefixes)
dbus-send --session --print-reply \
  --dest=org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.setCurrentDesktop int32:3

# Get a property
dbus-send --session --print-reply \
  --dest=org.kde.KWin /KWin \
  org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.Get \
  string:"org.kde.KWin" string:"currentDesktop"

# Monitor all D-Bus traffic (useful for discovering signals)
dbus-monitor --session

# Monitor a specific interface
dbus-monitor --session "interface='org.kde.KWin'"

@text
Applying Settings Changes

Many KDE settings require a reconfigure signal to take effect after editing rc files.

@code bash
# Reconfigure KWin (window manager settings)
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

# Reload Plasma shell (plasmashell settings)
qdbus org.kde.plasmashell /PlasmaShell org.kde.PlasmaShell.refreshCurrentShell

# Reload global shortcuts
# Editing kglobalshortcutsrc requires kglobalaccel to notice:
kquitapp5 kglobalaccel && sleep 1 && kglobalaccel5 &

# Reload KDE daemon modules
qdbus org.kde.kded5 /kded reconfigure

# Force full Plasma reload (nuclear option)
kquitapp5 plasmashell && kstart5 plasmashell &
